    "It’s an Apple-Silicon Mac on Wi-Fi, which macOS can’t wake from sleep over the network without an Apple TV/HomePod acting as a Sleep Proxy.\n\nFix: on the Mac, open Vamp Host → Settings → turn on “Keep Mac Awake & Reachable” (so it never sleeps), or connect it via Ethernet. Tap “Wake anyway” to try regardless (works if a Sleep Proxy is on the network).": {},
